msgid "Load Shedding reference guide"
msgstr ""

msgid "This technology is considered {extension-status}."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In _experimental_ mode, early feedback is requested to mature the idea.\n"
"There is no guarantee of stability nor long term presence in the platform "
"until the solution matures.\n"
"Feedback is welcome on our https://groups.google.com/d/forum/quarkus-"
"dev[mailing list] or as issues in our https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"issues[GitHub issue tracker]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For a full list of possible statuses, check our https://quarkus.io/faq/#what-"
"are-the-extension-statuses[FAQ entry]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Load shedding is the practice of detecting service overload and rejecting "
"requests."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In Quarkus, the `quarkus-load-shedding` extension provides a load shedding "
"mechanism."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use the Load Shedding extension"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To use the load shedding extension, you need to add the `io.quarkus:quarkus-"
"load-shedding` extension to your project:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"No configuration is required, though the possible configuration options are "
"described below."
msgstr ""

msgid "The load shedding algorithm"
msgstr ""

msgid "The load shedding algorithm has 2 parts:"
msgstr ""

msgid "overload detection"
msgstr ""

msgid "priority load shedding (optional)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Overload detection"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To detect whether the current service is overloaded, an adaptation of TCP "
"Vegas is used."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The algorithm starts with 100 allowed concurrent requests.\n"
"For each request, it compares the number of current requests with the "
"allowed limit and if the limit is exceeded, an overload situation is "
"signalled."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If the limit is not exceeded, or if priority load shedding determines that "
"the request should not be rejected (see below), the request is allowed.\n"
"When it finishes, its duration is compared with the lowest duration seen so "
"far to estimate a queue size.\n"
"If the queue size is lower than _alpha_, the current limit is increased, but "
"only up to a given maximum, by default 1000.\n"
"If the queue size is greater than _beta_, the current limit is decreased.\n"
"Otherwise, the current limit is kept intact."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Alpha and beta are computed by multiplying the configurable constants with a "
"base 10 logarithm of the current limit."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"After some number of requests, which can be modified by configuring the "
"_probe_ factor, the lowest duration seen is reset to the last seen duration "
"of a request."
msgstr ""

msgid "Priority load shedding"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If an overload situation is signalled, priority load shedding is invoked."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By default, priority load shedding is enabled, which means a request is only "
"rejected if the current CPU load is high enough.\n"
"To determine whether a request should be rejected, 2 attributes are "
"considered:"
msgstr ""

msgid "request priority"
msgstr ""

msgid "request cohort"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"There are 5 statically defined priorities and 128 cohorts, which amounts to "
"640 request groups in total."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"After both priority and cohort are assigned to a request, a request group "
"number is computed: `group = priority * num_cohorts + cohort`.\n"
"Then, the group number is compared to a simple cubic function of current CPU "
"load, where `load` is a number between 0 and 1: `num_groups * (1 - load^3)`.\n"
"If the group number is higher, the request is rejected, otherwise it is "
"allowed even in an overload situation."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If priority load shedding is disabled, all requests are rejected in an "
"overload situation."
msgstr ""

msgid "Customizing request priority"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Priority is assigned by a `io.quarkus.load.shedding.RequestPrioritizer`.\n"
"There is 5 statically defined priorities in the `io.quarkus.load.shedding."
"RequestPriority` enum: `CRITICAL`, `IMPORTANT`, `NORMAL`, `BACKGROUND` and "
"`DEGRADED`.\n"
"By default, if no request prioritizer applies, the priority is assumed to be "
"`NORMAL`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"There is one default prioritizer which assigns the priority of `CRITICAL` to "
"requests to the non-application endpoints.\n"
"It declares no `@Priority`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It is possible to define custom implementations of the `RequestPrioritizer` "
"interface.\n"
"The implementations must be CDI beans, otherwise they are ignored.\n"
"The CDI rules of typesafe resolution must be followed.\n"
"That is, if multiple implementations exist with a different `@Priority` "
"value and some of them are ``@Alternative``s, only the alternatives with the "
"highest priority value are retained.\n"
"If no implementation is an alternative, all implementations are retained and "
"are sorted in descending `@Priority` order (highest priority value comes "
"first)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Customizing request cohort"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Cohort is assigned by a `io.quarkus.load.shedding.RequestClassifier`.\n"
"There is 128 statically defined cohorts, with the lowest number being 1 and "
"highest number being 128.\n"
"The classifier should return a number in this interval; if it does not, the "
"number is adjusted automatically."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"There is one default classifier which assigns a cohort based on a hash of "
"the remote IP address and current time, such that an IP address changes its "
"cohort roughly every hour.\n"
"It declares no `@Priority`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It is possible to define custom implementations of the `RequestClassifier` "
"interface.\n"
"The implementations must be CDI beans, otherwise they are ignored.\n"
"The CDI rules of typesafe resolution must be followed.\n"
"That is, if multiple implementations exist with a different `@Priority` "
"value and some of them are ``@Alternative``s, only the alternatives with the "
"highest priority value are retained.\n"
"If no implementation is an alternative, all implementations are retained and "
"are sorted in descending `@Priority` order (highest priority value comes "
"first)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Limitations"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The load shedding extension currently only applies to HTTP requests, and is "
"heavily skewed towards request/response network interactions.\n"
"This means that gRPC, WebSocket and other kinds of streaming over HTTP are "
"not supported.\n"
"Other \"entrypoints\" to Quarkus applications, such as messaging, are not "
"supported either."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Further, the load shedding implementation is currently rather basic and not "
"heavily tested in production.\n"
"Improvements may be necessary."
msgstr ""

